{"name":"Explosive Grey","hex":"#c4c4c4","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"explosive","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Able to, or likely to, explode.","Having the character of an explosion."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any explosive substance.","A plosive."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/explosive"},{"term":"grey","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray.","Synonym of coloured (pertaining to the mixed race of black and white)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grey"}],"entries":[{"title":"Explosive","blocks":[{"text":"An explosive is a reactive substance that contains a great amount of potential energy that can produce an explosion if released suddenly, usually accompanied by the production of light, heat, sound, and pressure. An explosive charge is a measured quantity of explosive material. The material may either be composed solely of one ingredient or be a mixture containing at least two substances. An explosive can be used together with mechanical or electronic components to manufacture a bomb."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/17._%D0%95%D0%BA%D1%81%D0%BF%D0%BB%D0%BE%D0%B7%D0%B8%D0%B2%D0%BD%D0%B8_%D1%81%D0%B2%D0%BE%D1%98%D1%81%D1%82%D0%B2%D0%B0_%D0%BD%D0%B0_%D1%82%D1%80%D0%B8_%D1%80%D0%B0%D0%B7%D0%BB%D0%B8%D1%87%D0%BD%D0%B8_%D1%82%D0%B8%D0%BF%D0%BE%D0%B2%D0%B8_%D0%B5%D0%BA%D1%81%D0%BF%D0%BB%D0%BE%D0%B7%D0%B8%D0%B2%D0%B8.webm/330px--17._%D0%95%D0%BA%D1%81%D0%BF%D0%BB%D0%BE%D0%B7%D0%B8%D0%B2%D0%BD%D0%B8_%D1%81%D0%B2%D0%BE%D1%98%D1%81%D1%82%D0%B2%D0%B0_%D0%BD%D0%B0_%D1%82%D1%80%D0%B8_%D1%80%D0%B0%D0%B7%D0%BB%D0%B8%D1%87%D0%BD%D0%B8_%D1%82%D0%B8%D0%BF%D0%BE%D0%B2%D0%B8_%D0%B5%D0%BA%D1%81%D0%BF%D0%BB%D0%BE%D0%B7%D0%B8%D0%B2%D0%B8.webm.jpg","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Explosive"},{"title":"Grey","blocks":[{"text":"Grey o